<title>JAPAN: Nippon Mining raises copper tags 10,000 yen/tonne.</title>
<headline>Nippon Mining raises copper tags 10,000 yen/tonne.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Mining and Metals Co said it raised its selling price for electrolytic copper by 10,000 yen to 350,000 yen per tonne, effective immediately.</p>
<p>Major Japanese smelters periodically review their selling prices, changing them in line with market prices and currency rates.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
